From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] staging: t2bce: handle an ERR_PTR from t2bce_core_device_get()

t2bce_core_device_get() does not return NULL when the T2 BCE core is
absent: with no core registered it returns ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER), and
while the core is being removed it returns ERR_PTR(-ENODEV). The only
non-error return is get_device(bce->dev), which is never NULL.

t2bce_ave_init() nevertheless tested the result with "if (!core_dev)"
and so accepted the error pointer as a valid parent for device_create().
device_add()/kobject_get() then dereferences the poisoned pointer and
oopses on any machine or VM that loads t2bce_ave without a bound T2:

  BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: fffffffffffffe37
  Oops: 0000 [#1] SMP NOPTI
  RIP: 0010:kobject_get+0xd/0x70
  ...
   device_add+0x8f/0x850
   t2bce_ave_init+0xb2/0xff0 [t2bce_ave]

The sibling t2bce_vhci driver already handles this with IS_ERR() and
PTR_ERR(); do the same here. Use IS_ERR_OR_NULL() so a NULL return is
also rejected, clear the field before the error cleanup path (which
deliberately does not call t2bce_core_device_put(), since that must not
be invoked on an ERR_PTR), and preserve PTR_ERR() so a load that races
the core probe fails cleanly with -EPROBE_DEFER instead of crashing.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c
@@ -65,8 +65,10 @@
 		goto err_class;
 	}
 	t2bce_ave->core_dev = t2bce_core_device_get();
-	if (!t2bce_ave->core_dev) {
-		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(t2bce_ave->core_dev)) {
+		ret = t2bce_ave->core_dev ?
+			PTR_ERR(t2bce_ave->core_dev) : -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		t2bce_ave->core_dev = NULL;
 		goto err_state;
 	}
 	t2bce_ave->dev = device_create(t2bce_ave_class, t2bce_ave->core_dev,
